// An orc archer: lean, hunched, green, in a brown cowl with its long ears
// out of it. Drawn from the user's reference (orc_archer_ref.png) itself:
// its pixels read off at its own grid, shrunk to 0.76 (44 cells hood to
// sole; then, hunched, too big beside the player: the rows and columns
// that said least taken out, every part the same ones, to 39), the colours its own, then cut into its hood and face (one amber
// eye in a dark socket, the jaw thrust out, a tusk), its torso (the cowl's
// cloth over its shoulders, a strap and buckle across the chest, the belt,
// the torn tabard: leather to what's worn over it), its near arm (in front:
// long, a dark wrap at the wrist, a big clawed hand), its far arm (behind,
// an iron pauldron on its shoulder) and the longbow slung on its back.
// Its legs aren't drawn here: they're its creature file's `legs` (legs.rs,
// `rig`: bent green legs in brown boots), and its run keeps in step with
// them (`in_step`). Drawing, it takes the bow off its back: the slung bow
// is tagged with the near arm (`front_arm`), so it goes while the arm
// that aims stands in, the bow in that hand. Facing right; the game
// mirrors it.
(
    size: (49, 45),
    feet: (20.5, 45),
    outline: (17, 18, 9),
